entries.english:
Peter Philipp [von Dernbach], Bischof zu Bamberg und Würzburg, grants to the brothers Franz Christoph and Hans Konrad von Rosenberg, as trustees for Franz Rudolf von Rosenberg’s minor sons Philipp Ludwig, Johann Hartmann, Franz, and Anton Philibert, the following properties as male fiefs:
- Thundorf Castle with all rights, appurtenances, and revenues, except only the farmstead;
- the deserted settlement of Ransbach, with its mill and farmstead and all rights and revenues;
- the villages of Theinfeld and Rothhausen, with all rights, holdings, and revenues there;
- an estate in Maßbach behind the churchyard;
- the estates in Poppenlauer;
- the estates in Ebertshausen;
- half of the tithe at Altenmünster;
- one third of the tithe at Oberlauringen;
- one eighth of the tithe at Alsleben;
- one quarter of the tithe at Ober- and Untereßfeld;
- the tithe at Abersfeld;
- a vineyard and two woods at Thundorf.
In addition, the bishop grants them the following properties, which had belonged outright to Veit Ulrich von Schaumberg and which he then enfeoffed to the Würzburg bishopric:
- the farmstead and vineyards at Thundorf;
- the lake at Weißensee;
- a fishing right in the Lauer below Maßbach;
- a fishing right in the Lauer within the Rothhausen district;
- three quarters of the mill at Rothhausen;
- two estates at Theinfeld;
- two freehold estates at Weichtungen;
- four rent-paying fiefs at Stadtlauringen;
- nine estates and eleven fiefs in Maßbach;
- the Brandmühle below Maßbach;
- five estates and four fiefs in Poppenlauer;
- three estates and one fief in Nüdlingen;
- one fief in Rannungen;
- a field estate in Hesselbach;
- a freehold farm, three smallholdings, and the old manor barn at Abersfeld;
- the Herlingsberg wood;
- the male fief at Prappach.
The feoffees purchased these properties from the brothers Georg Dietrich, Wilhelm Ludwig, Wilhelm Ulrich, Georg Wilhelm, Johann Sigmund, Johann Philipp, and Johann Wilhelm von Schaumberg.
Sealer: the bishop, with his privy seal.

Notes: Abstract (18th century).
